* Key relationships: Cone volume = (1/3) of cylinder with same base and height. Sphere volume = (2/3) of cylinder with same base and height (actually same radius and height equal to diameter).
* Remember to use the height perpendicular to the base for cones, not the slant height.
* When solving composite solid problems, draw a diagram to identify all components.
